## Gráficos de barras

### Entendendo o uso de stat = ""



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Dataframe com categorias (sem valores predefinidos)
df5 <- data.frame(categoria = c("A", "B", "B", "C", "C", "C"))

# Gráfico de barras com o valor padrão (stat = "count")
ggplot(df5, aes(x = categoria)) +
  geom_bar()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](ggplot2_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-13-1.png){width=672}
:::

```{.r .cell-code}
# Dataframe com valores predefinidos
df6 <- data.frame(
  categoria = c("A", "B", "C"),
  valor = c(10, 20, 15))

# Gráfico de barras com stat = "identity"
ggplot(df6, aes(x = categoria, y = valor)) +
  geom_bar(stat = "identity")
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](ggplot2_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-13-2.png){width=672}
:::
:::

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
df7 <- dados %>% 
  filter(year == 2007 & continent == "Americas")

ggplot(df7, aes(x = pop, y = country)) +
  geom_bar(stat = "identity")
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](ggplot2_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-14-1.png){width=672}
:::

```{.r .cell-code}
df8 <- dados %>% 
  filter(year == 2007 & continent == "Oceania")

ggplot(df8, aes(x = country, y = pop, color = lifeExp)) +
  geom_bar(stat = "identity", width = 0.5)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](ggplot2_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-14-2.png){width=672}
:::

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(df8, aes(x = country, y = pop, fill = lifeExp)) +
  geom_bar(stat = "identity", width = 0.2)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](ggplot2_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-14-3.png){width=672}
:::

```{.r .cell-code}
?diamonds
ggplot(data = diamonds, aes(x = cut, fill = clarity)) +
  geom_bar()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](ggplot2_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-14-4.png){width=672}
:::

```{.r .cell-code}
# Quando usar position = "dodge"?

# Esse parâmetro é muito útil quando você tem uma variável adicional (como uma variável de agrupamento) e deseja visualizar as barras separadas, uma ao lado da outra, para comparar as diferentes categorias dentro de um grupo.

ggplot(data = diamonds, aes(x = cut, fill = clarity)) +
  geom_bar(position = "dodge")
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](ggplot2_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-14-5.png){width=672}
:::
:::



